# --- 🔄 Template Sync ---
#
# Every path tannergolden/repo ships, and whether 🔄 Template Sync, when you run
# it, keeps it current in this repository. How it all works:
# .github/template-sync.md, beside this.
#
# A line naming a path keeps it current. A `#` with no space before a path -
# `#/README.md` - leaves that path to you. A line starting `# ` is a note.
#
# To keep a file as yours, put a `#` in front of its line; to have the
# template keep it current again, take the `#` away. Rules of your own - a
# pattern like `!/.github/docs/**` to stop a whole folder - go under "Your
# rules" at the end, and win over everything above them. Each sync redraws
# this file from the template's latest list and keeps every choice you made
# in it.
#
# To keep your own lines in one file and still take the template's other
# changes to it, write a note under "Your rules" naming it, such as
# `# keep mine: /.github/workflows/checks.yml`. Where you and the template
# changed the same lines, yours then stand.

